<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.Africa gold industry in wage, productivity deal.</title>
<headline>S.Africa gold industry in wage, productivity deal.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's Chamber of Mines employer group said on Monday it had agreed an outline two-year wage and productivity accord with the National Union of Mineworkers (NUM).  </p>
<p>The agreement aims to increase annual gold production by 90 tonnes, the chamber added. South Africa's gold production in 1996 was 495 tonnes, the lowest in 40 years.</p>
<p>The interim deal is subject to negotiation and approval at mine and company level between management and union representatives. The aim is to commence these mine level talks immediately.</p>
<p>Wages increases will be backdated to July 1.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
